Richard,

Could you put the minutes-access pitch on the agenda for the September 21 des=
k at 2:00 p.m.? I've attached v0.3 for the desk read and, separately, the Aug=
ust 6 workbook so you can follow the dates and recalculate all 14 responses.

Keith and I confirmed receipt of both September 9 follow-ups: MIN-26-041 has =
an acknowledgment and MIN-26-042 a counter intake slip. Neither has a substan=
tive response yet with minutes or an answer about their location. The 26-day =
median in the pitch is for first substantive responses to the 2025 requests; =
four of those were status notices rather than copies of minutes.

I'd like us to examine how far response times can take the story. They don't =
by themselves establish when the minutes were accessible or whether a legal r=
equirement was breached. The pitch sets out the records we still need before =
making either claim and asks whether to keep reporting.

Leslie

